=== plain-80: width 80, height 24, profile notty, dark, glyphs ascii, plain
# play firewall/alpine-runlevel --------------------------------$
$
# Note$
# Play mode, mocks: the Firewall screen proposed for slice 4,$
# drawn from what real code reads of a simulated host$
# (firewall.Incoming.Check, ufw.Read, pve.ReadFirewall,$
# sshd.ReadEffective, reload.ReadBound), Enable the real$
# steps.PlanUFWEnable on the real plan/apply engine. Install,$
# Disable, the runlevel and the profiles' plans are the$
# gallery's stand-ins, unit (b)'s to build. Nothing on this$
# machine changes: every command and file is the fake's, and its$
# record is shown when play ends.$
$
# Info: firewall/alpine-runlevel$
# web-01.example.net runs Alpine 3.24. ufw active, deny$
# incoming, allowing 22, ENABLED=yes, in no runlevel, so it does$
# not come back after a reboot (ufw.md §6, [I]). v0.3.2 ran rc-$
# update add ufw default. The Firewall row cannot see this$
# (check-firewall.md §6): the At boot row can.$
$
# UFW Firewall Configuration ###################################$
$
  [+] Firewall             Configured deny policy$
$
# ufw ----------------------------------------------------------$
$
  [+] Installed            Yes$
  [+] Status               Active$
  [+] Incoming policy      Deny$
  [ ] At boot              In no runlevel$
$
# SSH ----------------------------------------------------------$
$
  [+] [::]:22              Allowed$
  [+] 0.0.0.0:22           Allowed$
$
# Rules --------------------------------------------------------$
$
  [+] 22/tcp               Allow$
  [+] 22/tcp (v6)          Allow$
$
  Select an option$
$
   1) Enable firewall      Let SSH through, deny the rest$
   2) Application Profiles Add, remove, apply$
$
   0) Return$
$
  > Enter selection [0-2 or q]: 1$
$
# Enable Firewall ##############################################$
$
# ufw ----------------------------------------------------------$
$
  [+] Status               Active$
  [+] Incoming policy      Deny$
  [+] At boot              Yes$
$
   -  Start ufw at boot$
      ufw$
      $ rc-update add ufw default$
$
  Enable the firewall? [y/N, 0 or q]: y$
$
  [+] Start ufw at boot    Done$
$
# Operation Successful$
$
# UFW Firewall Configuration ###################################$
$
  [+] Firewall             Configured deny policy$
$
# ufw ----------------------------------------------------------$
$
  [+] Installed            Yes$
  [+] Status               Active$
  [+] Incoming policy      Deny$
  [+] At boot              Yes$
$
# SSH ----------------------------------------------------------$
$
  [+] [::]:22              Allowed$
  [+] 0.0.0.0:22           Allowed$
$
# Rules --------------------------------------------------------$
$
  [+] 22/tcp               Allow$
  [+] 22/tcp (v6)          Allow$
$
  Select an option$
$
   1) Disable firewall     Stop ufw (not recommended)$
   2) Application Profiles Add, remove, apply$
$
   0) Return$
$
  > Enter selection [0-2 or q]: 0$
$
# simulated system ---------------------------------------------$
$
# Info: firewall/alpine-runlevel$
# Recorded by the fake, not done: what each step ran on web-$
# 01.example.net, and the files it changed, in order; hardn's$
# own journal, run directory and backups left out.$
$
   -  Applied: Start ufw at boot$
      $ rc-update add ufw default$
$

